  "purpose": "Artifacts captured at a known-good commit and never regenerated. The artifact bytes are identical to v0.2.0; what changed is how an execution result is recorded. v0.2.0 stored output as a text string, which DETERMINISTIC_SEMANTICS.md section 5 says is wrong: output is bytes and carries no encoding. This corpus records the canonical result form instead.",
  "migration_from_v0.2.0": [
    "v0.2.0 remains in the tree, byte-identical, and its artifact digests are still checked.",
    "Its recorded `execution` field used output as text and is superseded, not corrected in place.",
    "Each artifact here carries `canonical_result` plus the exact canonical JSON string, so a second implementation can compare bytes rather than re-deriving the serialization.",
    "The execution profile is recorded, because a result without its profile is not comparable."
  ],
  "rules": [
    "Never regenerate these files to make a test pass.",
    "A failure here is either a real regression or a deliberate format change.",
    "A deliberate change gets a NEW corpus directory plus a documented migration; this one stays."
  ],
